# Black Hole Manipulation

This project simulates the manipulation of a black hole using hand gestures. Users can control the size, speed, number of stars, colors, and more by using their fingers. It leverages machine learning for hand detection with the `ml5.js` Handpose model, and the simulation visualizes the effects of finger gestures on the black hole and stars.

## Controls

- **Auto-Refresh**: Press the button and then press **Play**.
- **Hand Gestures**:
  - **Red Stars**: Hold up **Index** & **Pinky**.
  - **Blue Stars**: Hold up **Thumb**, **Index**, & **Pinky**.
- **Pause Simulation**: Press the **Pause** button in the top left.
- **Toggle Camera**: Press the **Toggle Video** button or press **V** to toggle the camera.
- **Rainbow Trails**: Press the **Rainbow Trail** button to toggle rainbow trails.
- **Star Trails Length**: Use the slider at the bottom to change the length of the star trails.

## Description

This is an interactive black hole simulation. By using your hand, you can manipulate various aspects of the black hole and stars:
- The more fingers you hold up, the larger the black holes center of mass.
- You can toggle between red, blue, or rainbow trails for the stars.
- The black holes behavior changes based on the number of raised fingers.

## Features

- **Hand Tracking**: The simulation uses real-time hand tracking via `ml5.js`s Handpose model to detect gestures.
- **Interactive Star Effects**: Users can influence the star patterns and trails around the black hole.
- **Dynamic Black Hole**: The size and properties of the black hole adjust in real time based on the number of fingers held up.
- **Video Overlay**: Toggle the video stream of your hand gesture input.

## Run
- Click this link and make sure 'auto refresh' is turned on
- Press the play button
  [Final Project](https://editor.p5js.org/MatthewBoden/sketches/nWDu9yRza)

## Libraries Used

- **p5.js**: A JavaScript library for creative coding.
- **ml5.js**: A library for machine learning in the browser, used here for hand pose detection.
- **p5.gui**: A simple interface for creating GUI elements.

## How it Works

1. The `ml5.js` Handpose model is used to detect and track hand gestures.
2. The number of raised fingers and their combinations influence various properties of the black hole and stars:
   - The number of raised fingers adjusts the size of the black hole.
   - Different gestures change the colour and trail effects of the stars.
3. The simulation uses `p5.js` to visualize the black hole, stars, and hand gesture inputs.
